{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And behold the sun and the moon, etc.</b> Bereshit Rabbah: When Joshua said to the sun, 'Sun, in Gibeon stand still,' it did not want to stand until he said to it: 'And was it not your father's purchase?' — that is, are you not the servant of Joseph, as it is written: ״והנה השמש והירח ואחד עשר כוכבים משתחוים לי״? And Joshua was of the seed of Joseph, as it is written: ״למטה אפרים הושע בן נון״. Immediately: ״ויעמוד השמש״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase 'ולאו כסף זביניה דאבא' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'was it not your father's purchase.' The drift is the sun's refusing service until Joshua invokes Joseph's dream."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:32.744976504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}